  "question": {
    "text": "A real image is formed by a convex lens. If we put a concave lens in contact with it, the combination again forms a real image. The new image",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "IxzWk",
      "text": "is closer to the lens system",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iZ0mz",
      "text": "is farther from the lens system",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b3Daq",
      "text": "is at the original position",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "llyVx",
      "text": "may be anywhere depending on the focal length of the concave lens.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When concave lens is put in contact with convex lens, real/image is formed i.e., equivalent lens is convex. The focal length of equivalent lens F is greater than focal length of convex lens.<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />As f increases, <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> decreases<br /><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> also decreases<br /><br />Thus, v increases.",
